// Typecheck project for scripts/, EXCEPT the browser harnesses.
//
// Everything here runs under Bun on a terminal: migrations, backfills, puzzle
// tooling, the test runner itself. So it inherits the server project's
// settings, DOM deliberately EXCLUDED - a reference to `document` in a
// migration script is a bug, and leaving DOM out is what makes it one.
//
// scripts/browser-harness/ is the exception and has its own project,
// tsconfig.harness.json, because those files DO write browser code. DOM cannot
// simply be widened into this project to cover them: with lib.dom loaded, the
// DOM's ReadableStream shadows Bun's, and `for await (const chunk of
// proc.stderr)` in bgs-engine-probe.ts fails TS2504 because the DOM type
// declares no [Symbol.asyncIterator]. Measured 2026-08-09: no DOM here plus DOM
// there is 0 errors; one project with DOM for everything is 1, and the only way
// to silence it is a cast at a line that is already correct.
//
// scripts/**/*.mjs is not listed. Those are plain-JS harnesses with no types
// to check; eslint covers them for syntax and unused bindings.
//
// Read by two things, which must stay in step: `bun run typecheck`, and the
// type-aware ESLint rules in eslint.config.js.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.server.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.scripts.tsbuildinfo"
  },
  "include": ["scripts/**/*.ts", "scripts/**/*.mts"],
  "exclude": ["scripts/browser-harness/**"]
}
